<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barrak ibn Ghurayr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1682">1682</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barrak ibn Ghurayr was chief of the Banu Khalid, the leading tribal confederation of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. In 1670 he expelled the Ottoman garrison from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Hasa</a> and founded the Banu Khalid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a>, with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hofuf">Hofuf</a>. His family controlled the coast from Kuwait to Qatar and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> of the region for about a century, until the first Saudi state rose.</p></div>
